From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: clavin <clavin@electronjs.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: chore: disable BeginFrameArgs unthrottled_interval DCHECK on macOS

https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8664700
re-enabled this DCHECK on macOS. It still fires when
ExternalBeginFrameSourceMac has no usable display and falls back to its
DelayBasedTimeSource: GetMissedBeginFrameArgs() then pairs the timer's
preferred_interval_ with a longer min_refresh_interval_. Headless macOS
CI runners take that path, and three DCHECKs in a row make the browser
abort with "GPU process isn't usable".

This restores the upstream macOS exclusion. It can be removed once the
timer fallback keeps the two intervals consistent.

diff --git a/components/viz/common/frame_sinks/begin_frame_args.cc b/components/viz/common/frame_sinks/begin_frame_args.cc
index f170cb9cefad6f9620866798eb4d40d30fb9bb0e..c8542b0af0a38880035f8aefdee0a46b76a5ee7b 100644
--- a/components/viz/common/frame_sinks/begin_frame_args.cc
+++ b/components/viz/common/frame_sinks/begin_frame_args.cc
@@ -131,7 +131,11 @@ BeginFrameArgs::BeginFrameArgs(uint64_t source_id,
       frame_id(BeginFrameId(source_id, sequence_number)),
       type(type) {
   DCHECK_LE(kStartingFrameNumber, sequence_number);
-#if !BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
+#if !BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) && !BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
+  // TODO(crbug.com/477242770): Re-enable on Mac. Changing the system display
+  // refresh rate on macOS causes the unthrottled_interval state to go
+  // stale, which incorrectly trips this DCHECK.
+  //
   // TODO(crbug.com/477617022): Re-enable on Android.
   // ExternalBeginFrameSourceAndroid currently does not implement
   // GetMinimumFrameInterval() causing unthrottled_interval to always be
